# Normalise line endings.
#
# Five theme CSS files had drifted into mixed CRLF/LF — CRLF originally, with LF
# lines appended by later edits on other platforms. That is a quiet trap for
# contributors: the moment an editor normalises on save, a one-line theme tweak
# becomes a whole-file diff, which buries the actual change and makes review
# guesswork. Editing those files safely meant byte-level insertion that reused
# each anchor line's own terminator, which is not a reasonable thing to expect of
# anyone sending a PR.
#
# Nothing in the tree needs CRLF: there are no .bat/.cmd/.ps1 files checked in
# (the Windows uninstall cleanup script is generated at runtime).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never guess at these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.node binary
*.vsix binary
